description:
Design a 32-bit arithmetic shift module that performs a right arithmetic shift on the input `data` by a specified number of positions defined by `distance`. The leftmost bits of the result are filled with the sign bit of the input data to maintain the sign of the value being shifted, ensuring that the operation behaves correctly for signed numbers.
module top_module(
  input [31:0] data,
  input [3:0] distance,
  output [31:0] result
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [31:0] data,
  input [3:0] distance,
  output [31:0] result
);// Perform arithmetic left shift using << operator
  // Fill leftmost bits with sign bit of input data
  assign result = (data >>> {distance, {28{data[31]}}}) << distance;

endmodule

