description:
Design a Reed-Solomon coding module that performs encoding and decoding of a data stream. The module takes a k-bit input data symbol and outputs an n-bit encoded message, with the capability to correct up to t errors. The encoding process initializes the output with data values and applies a polynomial transformation based on the input, while the decoding process reconstructs the original data by employing a simplified inverse transformation. This implementation serves to enhance data integrity in communication systems by adding redundancy for error correction.
module top_module(
  input [k-1:0] d,
  output [n-1:0] c,
  output [k-1:0] d_
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [k-1:0] d,
  output [n-1:0] c,
  output [k-1:0] d_
);parameter n = 24; // length of encoded message
parameter k = 12; // number of data symbols
parameter t = 3; // number of errors that can be corrected

// Reed-Solomon encoding and decoding algorithms
// Note: This is a simplified version of the algorithms for demonstration purposes.
// In a real-world implementation, you would need to use more advanced algorithms
// and techniques for better error correction performance.

// Encoding algorithm
genvar i, j;
generate
  for (i = 0; i < n; i = i + 1) begin : encoding
    assign c[i] = (i < k) ? d[i] : 0;
    for (j = 0; j < k; j = j + 1) begin
      assign c[i] = (i >= k) ? c[i] ^ (d[j] * (i - k + 1)) : c[i];
    end
  end
endgenerate

// Decoding algorithm
generate
  for (i = 0; i < k; i = i + 1) begin : decoding
    assign d_[i] = 0;
    for (j = 0; j < n; j = j + 1) begin
      assign d_[i] = d_[i] ^ (c[j] * (j + 1));
    end
  end
endgenerate

endmodule

