description:
Design a reset synchronizer circuit that takes an active-low asynchronous reset signal (reset_n) and synchronizes it to the clock (clk). The output (reset) is a registered signal that ensures a clean and safe transition of the reset state, eliminating any metastability issues. The module captures the reset signal across two clock cycles and generates a synchronized reset signal that is asserted only when the asynchronous reset is low for at least one clock cycle.
module top_module(
  input reset_n,
  input clk,
  output reset
);

code:
module top_module(
  input reset_n,
  input clk,
  output reset
);reg reset_synced;
  reg [1:0] reset_synced_d;

  always @(posedge clk) begin
    reset_synced_d <= {reset_synced, reset_n};
    reset_synced <= reset_synced_d[1] & ~reset_synced_d[0];
  end

  assign reset = reset_synced;

endmodule

