description:
Design a rising edge detector circuit that outputs a high signal when a transition from low to high is detected on the input signal (IN) during the positive edge of the clock (CLK). The output (OUT) will be set to high (1) for one clock cycle whenever IN changes from low (0) to high (1), and otherwise, it remains low (0). The circuit utilizes a flip-flop structure to store the previous state of the input (last_IN) for edge detection purposes.
module top_module(
    input  wire IN,
    input  wire CLK,
    output reg  OUT
);

code:
module top_module(
    input  wire IN,
    input  wire CLK,
    output reg  OUT
);reg last_IN;

    always @(posedge CLK) begin
        if (IN && !last_IN) begin
            OUT <= 1'b1;
        end else begin
            OUT <= 1'b0;
        end
        last_IN <= IN;
    end

endmodule

